WEBVTT

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.120
Enemy analysis complete.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.620
Now heading to the Gate of No Retreat.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.280
Thanks to you all, I was able to take control of all the enemy's new mechs.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.380
I appreciate it.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.880
Wh-What are you saying?

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.390
Intelligence leaks.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.140
The time, scale,

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.250
and routes for our operation...

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.760
You've been leaking them this whole time, so I took advantage of it.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:45.640
What?

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.920
What are you talking about?

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.960
Are you seriously saying that?

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.440
We were simply getting rid of a traitor who defied national policy!

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.710
So you people are willing to sell out

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:02.290
your country to knock me down a peg?

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:05.360
We're looking at the bigger picture.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.420
You wouldn't understand.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.040
That's right!

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:10.860
Hey, now.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.790
Anyway, I've learned that you guys have no intention of winning the war.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.540
Do it.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.390
Wha—

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:25.690
Kageyama-san,

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:30.350
your friends were quite the traitors.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:33.550
There's no way our military could win like that.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.570
No...

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:41.160
Okay, enough depressing stuff.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.490
I'm getting back to my soldier work.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:47.040
Enjoy yourself.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:14.900
Damn it!

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.490
Those are our new models!

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.420
Don't worry.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.650
We'll get you and Jamie-chan to Arge.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:41.850
That's right.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.680
The whole unit's disobeying orders, anyway.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.870
We might as well make a nice show of it.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:48.300
Thanks a lot!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.100
Counterattack
Counterattack

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.310
Sturm Beta's pilots were forcibly

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.220
removed from their cockpits.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.240
Some resisted, but were killed.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.720
This was planned.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.290
Right, Lontar?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.100
I was only following orders.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:40.550
I never thought this would happen.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:42.670
Yeah, right.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.930
No... Viltriveld seems to be very confused by this.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.310
I'm waiting for word from them.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.580
Here, this function.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.820
Remember when an enemy artillery blast shut down Argevollen?

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.120
I do remember that.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.380
You went to restart it.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.210
Ever since then, Argevollen should have had

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:11.390
a function to restart it from outside in the event of an emergency...

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.330
It didn't work this time, though?

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:14.330
Yeah.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.810
It looks like our link was cut.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:23.460
So basically, the enemy got between the pilot and the system and took it over, right?

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.470
The unmanned mechs were a big enough surprise.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:27.220
Now he's taking over the system?

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:30.380
It's a world I don't understand at all.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.730
I get it. "Me" is Samonji-san!

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:41.940
Captain Samonji is commanding all those Trail Kriegers?

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.160
He's controlling hundreds of mechs at a time...

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.090
That would drive you crazy.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:51.260
All Trail Kriegers are probably set to turn towards the commander unit.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:54.480
So that's what "Look at me" means?

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.310
Once somebody's looking at someone else,

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.000
it's hard to get them to look back at you.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:02.380
It doesn't matter how much you mean it.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.540
They won't accept that.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.820
That sounds like it comes from a lot of experience.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:10.130
Yeah, but we have to do it.

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:11.260
You're right.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:14.690
I'm inside the system, too.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.650
I should be able to do something.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.030
This is impressive.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:24.380
I can't believe he took over all the U-Link systems.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:30.160
I'd heard it was theoretically possible, but this is splendid.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:35.620
I'd thought that Arandas would surrender after the string of defeats,

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.630
but things are turning in a good direction.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:43.410
It looks like this war will still turn a profit for us.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.020
Let's continue our meeting.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:53.230
What will bring us the most profits in the future?

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.000
Hey, so where are you?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.240
In front of the Gate of No Retreat.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:59.920
Fighting?

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.620
As planned.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:02.540
I see.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.270
I might be a little late.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:07.440
I keep getting messages from people who

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.610
want to join us, and it's causing a traffic jam.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.470
We're getting the roads under control.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:18.180
Some people just want to back the winning horse, probably.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.460
It's kind of cowardly of them, but...

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.340
They're still useful.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:25.880
That's right.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:29.220
That's why we give honor to those who perform commendable service in battle.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.220
Loyalty isn't given freely.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.480
Only after you give them something will people start to think

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.800
about who should they be fighting for.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:41.650
That's supposed to be how you build a victorious army.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.730
Shall I end it before they get a chance to perform commendable service?

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.980
You're so stingy.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:51.490
Compared to the Great Wall, the Gate of No Retreat is just a skirmish.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:08.220
Well?

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.920
Looking at it now.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:11.550
What's going on?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.710
We've got our basic plan.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.710
The rest is up to you two.

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:17.770
That's right.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:19.680
We're in the way...

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.500
So you take our place.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.940
Have fun!

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.150
Not that you'll have the time.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:35.340
A system check?

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.580
I'll use the method I used to look

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:42.370
directly inside Arge's systems, and make it look at me.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.750
Look at you?

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.830
You will face Arge with me.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.090
With you?

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:52.160
You and I are inside Arge's systems.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:55.370
It's only really Argevollen if the two of us are there!

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.860
We'll tell her!

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:58.320
Her?

00:08:58.320 --> 00:08:59.680
Can we do that?

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:03.110
Until now, all I've done is boot it up,

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:04.190
but now...

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:05.100
But now?

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.300
I'll face her.

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:08.360
Face her?

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:12.660
The first time, you and I made Argevollen move together.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.270
We can do it! I know!

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:17.360
Amazing.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.560
You sound like you can really do this.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.850
Not that I really understand what you're saying.

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.880
Idiot.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.440
Okay, let's start figuring out our plan.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.210
Look at Argevollen's manual.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:30.380
Okay!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.690
It feels like we're right there with them!

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:34.630
What is it?

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:36.910
The two of them are going to face it...

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.890
In other words, they're exposing everything they have, right?

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:42.770
Tokimune's an idiot, so he's fine.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:46.270
But that means Jamie will be showing everything that's in her heart.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:50.520
The greatest platonic relationship in history?

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.410
It sounds like they're talking about romance.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:56.270
Will it really work?

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.910
We need it to work.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.240
Damn it!

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:25.400
I'm intercepting radio traffic from Cayenne's forces.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.280
The unmanned squad has entered the Gate of No Retreat.

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:29.650
They're that far already?

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:30.440
They're fast.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.530
They've passed through the Gate!

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:34.140
Next is the Great Wall, right?

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:35.340
Yes.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:38.200
They're moving faster than I thought.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.890
But this is within expected parameters.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.200
Is it?

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:43.630
Yes.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:46.640
No matter how fast they are, they're still Kriegers.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:49.020
We'll go around to the side and flank them.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.960
Contact Seeker ahead of us.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.930
Tell him to get to the Great Wall as soon as possible.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:54.960
Roger.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:58.660
When the unmanned squad begins its attack on the Great Wall,

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:00.240
that'll be our chance.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.560
That will slow their advance.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:03.720
Let's roll out.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.320
We'll do our last tune-up on the canyon road.

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:07.980
I'll send out the Sekiei and Seiran.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:08.730
Roger!

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:17.570
Enemy sighted!

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:21.070
The new models, as well as the captured Sturm Betas!

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.080
Don't let them get any closer!

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.230
How did they get this close?

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:28.330
I thought they were still at point 03!

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.100
All units, split up.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:31.250
Commence attack.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.140
Advance before they fire their next round.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.320
Don't bunch up.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:48.640
Spread out their targets.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:13.170
When we took over, we set up several artillery batteries.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:15.210
Hard to attack.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.720
Easy to defend.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:22.530
The Arandas forces would never approach the Great Wall.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:24.180
But that was...

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:28.670
Only true if the Perfevollens didn't exist, right?

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:32.690
Argevollen.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:05.170
Hey.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:08.550
Thanks to you, it's gone just fine so far.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.770
But this is where it gets hard.

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:13.700
It's awfully crowded on this narrow road.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:17.350
It's like attacking on a tightrope.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:20.070
If you don't move faster, more soldiers will die.

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:25.070
You're free to stay in the back and watch.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:26.240
Idiot.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:29.630
I'll put two mechanized infantry units on your flanks.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:31.080
Work with them when you fight.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:34.630
Your army may not die, but if it breaks, it's useless.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.860
I can't have you dying now.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:38.250
We've got a long way to go.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.590
Obey your commanding officer's orders.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:41.590
Understood.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.090
These are the orders from Lieutenant Holmes.

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:46.540
I see.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.500
An enemy mech that appears

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.100
to be Argevollen was sighted in the enemy unit.

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:52.810
Argevollen?

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:05.100
I tried connecting the terminal to the Sekiei's display.

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:07.540
It's so big and easy to see!

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:08.320
Thanks!

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:11.130
I tweaked the output a little.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:14.460
It's got a bit of a temper now, though not as much as Argevollen.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:16.100
Sounds fine to me!

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.080
Let's go!

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:17.710
Right!

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.050
They left!

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:27.650
Hurry! Hurry!

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:30.680
You there, Akane-chan?

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.700
I'm still busy.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:36.880
When this is over, let's go get something to eat.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:37.670
Bye.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:40.070
He really never changes.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:41.850
Right, Akane?

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:43.890
But this is the first time he's asked me out.

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:45.220
Before a mission.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:49.230
Come back safe, darling!

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:50.710
It's progressed that far?

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:51.950
They're husband and wife now?

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:55.300
Hey, playboy.

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:56.950
What are you doing at a time like this?

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:00.640
Don't you always use closed lines?

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:03.880
I thought it might be nice to be open for once.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:04.890
Let's go.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:05.980
Right, right.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.940
So it was Akane-san, huh?

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.220
That's a bit of a surprise.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.470
I think they might actually make a good couple.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.400
Captain Suzushiro.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:26.430
What is it?

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:31.490
We're currently passing through the place where I met Argevollen, right?

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:33.550
That's right.

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:36.980
Everything began when you got inside Argevollen.

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:41.840
Because Jamie and I activated Arge back then,

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:46.420
we may be able to take it back now.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:52.190
When we were talking about that, I got to thinking about something.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:56.890
I heard something when he told me to get out of Arge.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.030
Heard what?

00:15:58.030 --> 00:15:59.800
Another open line?

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:00.430
Shh!

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.500
He told me...

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.690
Survive.

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:08.750
That's what he said?

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:11.130
That's what it sounded like to me.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.590
So I can still hear it in my mind.

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:18.560
At the time, it sounded to me like a selfish excuse.

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:22.860
But now that I'm trying to take Arge back,

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.790
that seems wrong.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.760
Survive.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:34.640
Point 03 was penetrated.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:38.430
Multiple enemy mechs have rendezvoused with the unmanned squad.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.490
They're fighting on the front lines.

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:47.150
I'm sure they never thought they'd be destroying their own fortress.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.390
Their numbers are limited.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:54.660
If we can defeat them and crush them, we can win.

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.570
They're already this far?

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:04.540
But the way they're fighting is odd.

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:09.240
Even if the unmanned mechs aren't alive, it's a human commanding them.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:11.550
But there's too little uncertainty in the way he's fighting.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:22.960
Almost there!

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.910
Reinforcements are still coming!

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.560
The tide is turning.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.610
The tide?

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.200
That's right.

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:34.100
I'm taking control of the tide and letting you rewrite the script.

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:36.140
They're businessmen.

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:38.390
They know what's best.

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:40.280
You're confident.

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:43.290
No. I'm certain.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:44.760
Retreat?

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.490
What do you mean?

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:48.490
Just what I said.

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:51.870
The Great Wall's defenders will open all gates and withdraw.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.300
We're retreating.

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:56.920
We need to maintain the Great Wall to keep

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:58.940
Ingelmia's supply lines open!

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:01.090
For the coming invasion...

00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:05.430
I don't know if that invasion is ever coming.

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:11.650
Junios just had a parade,

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:15.640
but Central Command's opinion on the invasion is actually rather pessimistic.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.070
Th-That's...

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:20.140
We aren't losing.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:24.830
Fighting where defending it to the death means nothing is meaningless.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.960
Additional enemy reinforcements are approaching.

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:33.420
But if we don't defend the Great Wall to the death, the rest of the war...

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:36.360
Who are we fighting this war for?

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:40.610
Excuse me.

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:46.920
Yes, I just made the same proposal.

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:48.710
Yes.

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:50.200
Yes.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.150
Goodbye.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:56.440
You're right, Lt. Colonel Holmes.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.530
I support the retreat.

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.900
This is Lt. Colonel Holmes.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:07.160
We are abandoning the Great Wall.

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:10.170
Formations 3 and 4 are to

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.730
delay the enemy advance as long as possible.

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:16.380
The rear forces at the center are to support those at the far rear.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:19.160
Remaining forces are to execute a fighting withdrawal.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:21.390
I know you'll all fight bravely.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:23.390
Retreat! We're retreating!

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:25.680
We're leaving the Great Wall!

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.650
This is Seeker.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.650
The enemy is retreating.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:36.530
They're leaving.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:40.280
Captain Suzushiro.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.380
It's too soon.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:46.080
If Samonji-san gets inside the Great Wall, we can't get close.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.000
Understood.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.170
What is it?

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:50.790
The enemy is retreating.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.420
Our allies are getting inside the base.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.670
Let's hurry!

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.160
Hey, Tokimune!

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:02.780
There are people behind you!

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:05.900
The chief's tuning makes us go fast!

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:07.310
Okui-san...

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:11.160
Our job is to connect Tokimune and the Seiran!

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.310
Step on it!

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:36.280
The enemy is leaving this for us.

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:40.960
We'll use this as a base and regroup on the front lines.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.970
On the front lines, there is truth.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.410
There is power!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:50.220
We'll bring back victory and wipe out the lazy fools in the capital,

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:52.230
then strive for greater victory!

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:56.260
Samonji, this is where it gets real.

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:09.460
I'll show you a wider world.

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:17.590
Activate Fascinator.

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:37.190
What's going on?

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:38.690
Samonji...

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:45.950
What are you doing?

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:47.950
Samonji!

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.690
What's going on?

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:58.680
Why are they coming out?

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:00.100
That's not what was supposed to happen.

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:02.340
The path is decided.

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:06.600
Someone who intends to die doesn't need that unit.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.090
I'll take it.

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:10.970
What are you saying?

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:13.850
You're going to disobey Central Command, Viltriveld?

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:15.180
I don't really care.

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:16.780
You...

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:26.120
The unmanned mechs are the cornerstone of my future,

00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:28.200
the key to my long-held desire.

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:29.530
We'll intercept them.

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:30.780
Yes, sir!

00:22:33.230 --> 00:22:35.790
He's trying to turn back time,

00:22:36.490 --> 00:22:38.840
to before he met Argevollen...

00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:42.360
In exchange for his own life...

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:54.060
I was right. I have to stop him.

00:22:55.890 --> 00:22:58.560
He only thinks about himself.

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:01.130
He doesn't think about anybody else.

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:05.160
Not about me, or my sister, or Captain Suzushiro...

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:07.390
So I'm going to stop him!

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:09.320
I'm going to take back Arge!

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:10.410
That's right.

00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:12.300
Let's stop him.

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:14.580
That's why we're here.

00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:17.330
Nobody wants this!

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:24.680
Ukyo Samonji!

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:40.070
Silver Will
